# RevYield — environment template
#
# Copy to .env and paste your own connection string. .env is git-ignored;
# this file is the only one that ships.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Neon gives you TWO connection strings. Use the DIRECT one, not the pooled one.
# The pooled endpoint has "-pooler" in the host and runs PgBouncer in transaction
# mode, which is the wrong shape for what seed_data.py does: multi-statement DDL
# and four COPY streams inside a single transaction. The direct endpoint handles
# both. Once the data is loaded, the pooled endpoint is fine for Power BI.
#
# sslmode=require is appended automatically if you leave it off — Neon refuses
# non-SSL connections. Keep it explicit anyway; it documents intent.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<user>:<password>@ep-<id>.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
